# PROFILE D — C, plus two risk-per-trade gates. Nothing about signal generation,
# entries or exits changes; only how much is bought once a signal fires.
#
# WHY. On 2026-08-04 the strategy traded 09:30-10:08 IST and was then halted by the
# daily loss limit (1,670 signals suppressed). In that window:
#
#   SENSEX PE   0 wins /  7   gross -18,674     <- the whole loss, and then some
#   SENSEX CE   3 wins /  7   gross  +4,196
#   NIFTY  CE   8 wins / 28   gross  +2,301
#   NIFTY  PE   4 wins / 10   gross    +975
#
# The losing leg was not wrong more OFTEN -- sorted by entry premium instead:
#
#   premium     n   win%   mean %move   mean notional
#   < Rs 25    18    16%       -1.67%        Rs   2,000
#   25-150     20    55%       +2.34%        Rs  23,960
#   150-400    10    10%       -0.48%        Rs  58,418
#   > Rs 400    4     0%       -2.94%        Rs 122,331
#
# Fixed lots make risk proportional to premium. "5 lots NIFTY / 10 lots SENSEX"
# sounds uniform but notional ran 2,000 -> 122,331, a 60x spread. The edge lives in
# convexity (the two winning near-ATM calls moved +11% and +13%); deep-ITM legs have
# delta near 1 and no convexity, so lot-based sizing put the most capital exactly
# where there was none.
#
# Replaying 2026-08-04 with the same signals, entries and exits:
#
#   baseline (what actually ran)   52 trades          NET -16,560
#   D: cap 50k + min premium 20    34 trades          NET  -1,550
#   cap 50k alone                  52 trades          NET  -3,058
#   min premium 20 alone           34 trades          NET -15,051
#
# The cap does almost all the work; the premium floor mostly removes trades that
# were never able to pay for themselves (14 entries under Rs 10 produced -211 gross
# against Rs 694 of charges, and 5 trades had gross of exactly Rs 0.00).

ANALYZE_SEGMENTS=NSE_FO,BSE_FO,NSE_EQ
ANALYZE_MONEYNESS=ATM,OTM
SHORT_SEGMENTS=NSE_EQ,BSE_EQ
EXIT_STOP_SIGMA=4.0
EXIT_TRAIL_SIGMA=2.0
EXIT_TARGET_PCT=0
EXIT_MAX_HOLD_SECS=3600
ANGLE_Q=0.95
MAX_OPEN_POSITIONS=20
EQUITY_MARGIN_PER_TRADE=20000
EQUITY_LEVERAGE=5

# Cap notional per trade. Rounds DOWN to a whole lot -- options cannot be traded in
# fractions, and 0 lots means the cap is refusing the trade rather than guessing.
# Rs 50,000 is chosen to sit ABOVE every trade that made money on 4 Aug (the largest
# winner was Rs 27,274) so the cap cuts losers without touching winners on the day
# it was derived from. Rs 35,000 scores better on that day (NET +3,059) but that is
# fitted to a single 38-minute window -- do not adopt it on this evidence.
MAX_NOTIONAL_PER_TRADE=50000

# Refuse entries below this premium. At Rs 0.15 the Rs 0.05 tick is a 33% move, so
# the angle is measuring quantisation, not geometry.
MIN_PREMIUM=20

# NOTE ON READING THE RESULT. The 4 Aug loss limit fired 38 minutes in, so that day
# is one small sample, not a session. If D looks better, first check WHETHER IT
# TRADED ALL DAY -- smaller positions mean the limit is hit later or not at all, and
# a longer sample is the main thing being bought here, not a better win rate.
# Holding time remains the only discriminator stable across three sessions:
# <30s = 0% win, >10min = 50%. Signal strength is still not predictive.
